# Mimi — AI Agent Desktop App

A desktop AI assistant built on **Electron + React + TypeScript**, powered by **GitHub Copilot** models.
Mimi helps engineering teams analyze tickets, review commits, generate test cases, write weekly reports, and query internal knowledge stored in a local vector database.

---

## Features

- **Chat interface** — streaming responses with full Markdown & code-block rendering
- **GitHub Copilot backend** — supports GPT-4o, GPT-4o Mini, o1, o3 and custom models
- **RAG / Vector memory** — ChromaDB stores and retrieves project requirements & documents
- **Tool use** — agent calls specialized tools (requirement lookup, ticket analysis, etc.)
- **Conversation history** — persisted sessions with sidebar navigation
- **Three themes** — Dark (Claude-style), Light (Gemini-style), System (deep ocean blue)
- **Quick prompts** — one-click starters for common engineering tasks

---

## Prerequisites

| Requirement           | Version                                         |
| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Node.js               | ≥ 18                                            |
| npm                   | ≥ 9                                             |
| ChromaDB              | running on `localhost:8000` (optional, for RAG) |
| GitHub Copilot access | valid token / OAuth                             |

---

## Development

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start in dev mode (hot-reload)
npm run dev
```

---

## Build

```bash
# Compile only (outputs to out/)
npm run build

# Package for current OS
npm run package

# Package for specific platform
npm run package:win     # Windows (.exe installer)
npm run package:mac     # macOS (.dmg)
npm run package:linux   # Linux (.AppImage)
```

Built artifacts are placed in the `dist/` folder.

---

## Project Structure

```
src/
  main/           # Electron main process
    agent/        # Copilot agent & client services
    data/         # Vector DB ingestion & memory
    ipc/          # IPC handlers
    services/     # Settings, conversation persistence
    tools/        # Agent tool definitions
  preload/        # Context bridge
  renderer/       # React UI (Vite)
    views/        # ChatView, HistoryView, SettingsView
    components/   # MessageBubble, InputBar, StatusBar …
    store/        # Zustand state (chat, settings)
    styles/       # Tailwind + CSS custom properties
  shared/         # Shared IPC types
```

---

## Configuration

Open **Settings** (gear icon in the sidebar) to configure the ChromaDB host and port.
Model and theme can be changed directly from the sidebar menu bar.
